  "note": "Annual election of six urban councillors, May 1939; the six retiring members withdrew and six candidates were returned unopposed (Belfast News-Letter, 8 May 1939, p. 9). The retiring members who withdrew were John Campbell, James M'Cartney, William Byrtt, Daniel Blair, W. J. M'Cune and John Gorman. Returned unopposed."
